{
  "_id": "tg-smite",
  "content": [
    {
      "text": "neither will I again smite any more every thing living, Gen. 8:21. he spied an Egyptian smiting an Hebrew, Ex. 2:11. Lord smote all the firstborn, Ex. 12:29. thou shalt smite the rock, Ex. 17:6 (Num. 20:11; 1 Ne. 17:29). He that smiteth a man, so that he die, shall be surely put to death, Ex. 21:12. Cursed be he that smiteth his neighbour secretly, Deut. 27:24. Lord shall smite thee with a consumption, Deut. 28:22. Saul sought to smite David even to the wall, 1 Sam. 19:10. Uzzah; and God smote him there for his error, 2 Sam. 6:7. retire ye from him, that he may be smitten, 2 Sam. 11:15. smote the waters, and they were divided, 2 Kgs. 2:8. angel … smote in the camp of the Assyrians, 2 Kgs. 19:35 (Isa. 37:36). he smote the rock, Ps. 78:20. smote great nations, Ps. 135:10. Let the righteous smite me, Ps. 141:5. Smite a scorner, and the simple will beware, Prov. 19:25. he shall smite thee with a rod, Isa. 10:24 (2 Ne. 20:24). he shall smite the earth with the rod of his mouth, Isa. 11:4 (2 Ne. 21:4; 30:9). neither shall the heat nor sun smite them, Isa. 49:10 (1 Ne. 21:10). I gave my back to the smiters, Isa. 50:6. we did esteem him stricken, smitten of God, Isa. 53:4 (Mosiah 14:4). ye fast … to smite with the fist of wickedness, Isa. 58:4. let us smite him with the tongue, Jer. 18:18. stone … smote the image upon his feet, Dan. 2:34. Ephraim is smitten, Hosea 9:16. I smote you with blasting and with mildew, Hag. 2:17. smite the shepherd, and the sheep shall be scattered, Zech. 13:7 (Matt. 26:31; Mark 14:27). Lord will smite all the people, Zech. 14:12. lest I come and smite the earth with a curse, Mal. 4:6 (3 Ne. 25:6; D&C 27:9; 110:15; 128:17; 138:48; JS—H 1:39).",
